{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/572576-beast-the-doorkicking","id":572576,"title":"Beast: The Doorkicking","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-29T06:10:25-07:00","id":572576,"title":"Beast: The Doorkicking","content":"This is just an idle passing thought, but one of the reasons that a given group of non-Beast supernaturals might be OK with letting one of them join the group is if they have enemies who can escape into a realm the group can't normally get into. To go with the OWoD cliche, a group of vampires trying to get a hostile werewolf pack out of town would get a TON of mileage out of having a buddy who can just smash open a gate into the Shadow for them.<br /> <br /> Just to get other peoples thoughts: how common is the knowledge that the Beasts have access to their Skeleton Key? I'd imagine they don't just go around telling everyone, but by the way the power is described it isn't exactly subtle, and people they're chasing must get away at least <i>some</i> of the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sisyphus has it easy...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1647-mechalith","name":"Mechalith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T08:39:46-07:00","id":572707,"title":"","content":"Well one thing I've gotten the impression of is that the Beghotten are a tricky group for other species to know a lot about as a whole. Not necessarily because the Beasts are exceptionally secretive and more because unless something corrects them most groups aren't going to look at 3 people who are a kraken, a leviathan, and siren and assume they're the same species of monster. Much less reach the conclusion that the dragon, wyvern, stone giant, and worm that walks are related without being told and probably getting a fair amount of proof.<br /> <br /> Depending on the story I'd list it as kind of an urban legend some splats have of things that seem to break gates, Kind of a case of just assuming that if you aren't sure what your opponent is don't assume your safe just because you managed to world jump.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T12:24:09-07:00","id":573021,"title":"","content":"Ehhhh.... too complicated.<br /> <br /> First, the supernatural in question (lets go with vampires, since they're the least alternative world mobile) has to pick a fight with another supernatural that has access to said otherworld (lets say mages, they've got access to all the places).<br /> <br /> So, mages are attacking vampires from the Hisil. What do we need to do to get to the mages on the other side?<br /> <br /> 1) Find beasts exist and approach them.<br /> 2) Find out that Beasts can use a skeleton key.<br /> 3) Convince Beasts to enter this attack, when they're just as likely to go neutral or join the mages.<br /> 4) find a locus that they can use said skeleton key on. Remember - Beasts do not naturally have any kind of location sense, so they're just as clueless as vampires when it comes to finding a locus.<br /> 4a) Talk to a mage, werewolf, or possibly prommie to lead the way to said locus<br /> 5) Deal with the native spirit threats<br /> 6) Launch a successful attack on another realm where they have no advantages or homeground expertise.<br /> <br /> <br /> As you can see, this is a highly lengthy and difficult process here. Skeleton key works great when the Beast needs to accompany someone else when they open a door to an otherworld and follow along, but as an offensive weapon for someone else to use?<br /> <br /> I suppose you could make a plot about it; playing interspecies diplomat is exactly the type of plot I can imagine Beast doing. So, Begotten PCs taking sides and offering such assistance is plausable. But from a vampire (or whatever other supernatural) point of view, I can't see them taking the initiative on the plan.<br /> <br /> Really, Skeleton Key is highly overrated. It -sounds- really good, but the practical limitation of not having a way to sense a locus, hallow, avernian gate, or trod really limits its effectiveness. Its great when you're teamed up with someone else that can show you where said gateways are; like, if the Beast wants to accompany Uratha on a hunt, or changelings want help picking hedge fruit. But random access to every realm? Doesn't really happen on its own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 06-29-2015, 03:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}